ising targets and revenue projections.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"1">I have=\
 drafted a follow-up email that acknowledges his feedback while summarizing=\
 the key points you discussed for his reference.</p><h3 data-path-to-node=\
=3D"2">Follow-up Email to Thad</h3><p data-path-to-node=3D"3"><b data-path-=\
to-node=3D"3" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Subject:</b> Re: Co-Founder / Chief =\
Operating Officer, OpenWorldTech.io</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"4">Hi Thad,<=\
/p><p data-path-to-node=3D"5">Thank you again for the time this morning. It=\
 was an incredibly interesting and enlightening chat=E2=80=94I really appre=\
ciate you sharing your perspective on the current venture landscape and bei=\
ng so candid with your feedback on our current positioning.</p><p data-path=\
-to-node=3D"6">As I mentioned, I=E2=80=99m jumping into the deep end on the=\
 corporate/fundraising side, so having a "pilot" with your experience to he=\
lp navigate these waters is exactly what I'm looking for. I jotted down a f=\
ew of the main points from our call for reference as we both consider the n=\
ext steps:</p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"7"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0=\
"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,0,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Fundraising Calib=\
ration:</b> You noted that our current $1M target is likely too low for the=\
 runway required in the current AI market. A $3M pre-seed round is a more r=\
ealistic "market-palpable" target to ensure we hit the necessary milestones=\
 for a Series A.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,1,0"><b data-path-to=\
-node=3D"7,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Cap Table &amp; Valuation:</b> We =\
discussed tightening the caps to ensure I don=E2=80=99t get "washed out" to=\
o early. Keeping founder ownership high (70-80% pre-Series A) is a priority=\
 for investor stability and my own long-term control.</p></li><li><p data-p=\
ath-to-node=3D"7,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"=\
0">Revenue Projections:</b> My initial $700k Year 2 projection is too conse=\
rvative for VCs looking for a unicorn trajectory. We need to model for a mo=\
re aggressive "scale-up" narrative (e.g., $1M Year 1 / $5M Year 2) to demon=\
strate the true market potential.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,3,0=\
"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,3,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Pitch Deck Refine=\
ment:</b> The deck needs to be less "global" and more specific. We need to =\
lead with the immediate problem (AI usability/integration) and the specific=\
 "initial market" we are capturing before talking about the broader ecosyst=\
em.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"7,4,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"7,4,=\
0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Operational Path:</b> We discussed the possibil=\
ity of an Advisory Board role (5-10 hours/week) vs. a full-time COO. This w=\
ould allow us to leverage your network and experience to close the seed rou=\
nd while the product is still in the "build" phase.</p></li></ul><p data-pa=\
th-to-node=3D"8">I=E2=80=99m really encouraged by your interest in the visi=\
on and your philosophy of "decisions in the best interest of the company." =\
I=E2=80=99ll look forward to hearing your thoughts in a few days once you=\
